# The security fix to dilla-media task 9, D(i): a member whose leaf the instance is already removing
# cannot post its own Remove of that leaf. Before the fix carol's own Remove voided the instance's,
# which lifted the freeze, ended the election and left nothing forcing a commit: a kicked member who
# kept re-posting its self-Remove stayed in the call, decrypting media. Now the delivery service
# refuses it (409 E_REMOVE_PENDING); the testkit's leave
# verb reads that refusal as "I am being removed", withdraws its own proposal and goes on. The call
# stays frozen. The Go test that runs this asserts the instance's Remove is still the one non-void
# proposal, that no member proposal reached the log and that the election stands.
instance dilla
client alice
client bob
client carol
group call kind=call target=e4e4e4e4e4e4e4e4e4e4e4e4e4e4e4e4 community=none creator=alice
join bob call via=external
sync alice
join carol call via=external
sync alice
sync bob
kick alice carol
leave carol call
expect_425 send alice call the kick still holds the call
